1
00:00:00,325 --> 00:00:02,112
If a shark ate you, would it
poop out your

2
00:00:02,112 --> 00:00:04,162
bones? First of all...

3
00:00:04,162 --> 00:00:05,750
terrible vacation.

4
00:00:05,750 --> 00:00:07,975
But don't picture a tiny
skeleton coming

5
00:00:07,975 --> 00:00:09,400
out the other end.

6
00:00:10,150 --> 00:00:13,450
A shark's digestive system can
break down bone.

7
00:00:13,450 --> 00:00:15,562
Large pieces that don't break
down may

8
00:00:15,562 --> 00:00:18,475
stay in the stomach and get
vomited back out.

9
00:00:19,275 --> 00:00:20,750
Yes. Wrong exit.

10
00:00:20,750 --> 00:00:22,900
And here's where it gets
ridiculous.

11
00:00:23,675 --> 00:00:25,550
Some sharks can push their
stomach out

12
00:00:25,550 --> 00:00:28,050
through their mouth, get rid of
unwanted

13
00:00:28,050 --> 00:00:31,000
material, then pull it back
inside.

14
00:00:31,750 --> 00:00:34,262
Imagine turning your stomach
inside out

15
00:00:34,262 --> 00:00:36,425
because lunch was being
difficult.

16
00:00:37,175 --> 00:00:40,625
So your bones don't have one
guaranteed destination.

17
00:00:40,625 --> 00:00:42,250
Some can break down.

18
00:00:42,250 --> 00:00:45,125
Stubborn pieces may get returned
to sender.

19
00:00:45,850 --> 00:00:47,225
Congratulations.

20
00:00:47,225 --> 00:00:48,588
You weren't just lunch.

21
00:00:48,588 --> 00:00:50,750
You were a customer service
issue.
